|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| **True splice sites** | |  |  |  |
| Donor sites, canonical (GT@301 or AC@298) | 666 | 1.000 (666/666) | 0.973 (648/666) | 0.866 (577/666) |
| Donor sites, non-canonical (neither motif) | 13 | 0.000 (0/13) [0.00–0.23] | 0.692 (9/13) [0.42–0.87] | 0.615 (8/13) [0.36–0.82] |
| Acceptor sites, canonical (AG@298 or CT@301) | 635 | 0.959 (609/635) | 0.943 (599/635) | 0.762 (484/635) |
| Acceptor sites, non-canonical (neither motif) | 0 | n/a | n/a | n/a |
| All splice sites, canonical | 1301 | 0.980 (1275/1301) | 0.958 (1247/1301) | 0.816 (1061/1301) |
| **All splice sites, non-canonical** | 13 | 0.000 (0/13) [0.00–0.23] | 0.692 (9/13) [0.42–0.87] | 0.615 (8/13) [0.36–0.82] |
| **Not splice sites** (correct = called *none*) | |  |  |  |
| Non-sites with a decoy motif at those offsets | 184 | 0.000 (0/184) | 0.609 (112/184) | 0.821 (151/184) |
| Non-sites with no motif at those offsets | 502 | 1.000 (502/502) | 0.958 (481/502) | 0.843 (423/502) |
- **Non-canonical sites are rare here:** 13 of 1314 true splice sites in these 2,000 test windows (6 GC donor (+ strand, GC@301), 6 GC donor (− strand, GC@298), 1 other). The rule gets every one of them wrong by construction.
- **NT-v2-50M** (`center_tok`) recovered **9/13** non-canonical sites (95% CI 0.42–0.87) and correctly rejected **112/184** decoy windows, where the rule is right on none of either group.
- **DNABERT-2** (`center_tok`) recovered **8/13** non-canonical sites (95% CI 0.36–0.82) and correctly rejected **151/184** decoy windows, where the rule is right on none of either group.
- The non-canonical group is too small to carry a strong claim on its own (see the interval). The decoy row is the larger piece of evidence: those windows contain exactly the motif the rule looks for, at exactly the right offset, and only context can tell that they are not splice sites.
